## 🌺 English Contemplation

A scripture is not exhausted because it has been read once.

We change.  
Our questions change.  
Our maturity changes.

Therefore the same sentence can meet us differently each time we return to it.

Repeated reading becomes reflection.  
Repeated reflection becomes practice.  
Practice purifies the inner instrument.  
And what remains unclear may still be placed at the feet of the Divine.

The seeker need not wait for perfect understanding before beginning.

Sometimes the path is simply:

**Read again.  
Remember again.  
Practice again.  
Surrender again.**

Until knowledge is no longer something merely remembered—

but something quietly lived.

